From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shanshan <samsom0409@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Oct 2026 01:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gmm: give GroupedMatmulSwigluQuantV2 a straight line at one workspace split

The A8W4 MSD schedule runs a three-stage software pipeline over
`workspaceSplitConfig.loopCount` chunks. At `loopCount == 1` the loop body
still issues the prefetch of a chunk that does not exist and the epilogue of
a chunk index of -1, and still executes four device barriers where the
correct sequence needs two.

Both dead calls return immediately -- `preProcess.Process` on
`workspaceSplitLoopIdx >= loopCount` and `postProcess.Process` on that or on
a negative index -- so they contribute nothing but the barriers built around
them. The `tempWorkspaceSplitConfig` the epilogue is handed on that first
iteration is zero rather than indeterminate, because every field of
`WorkSpaceSplitConfig` carries a default member initialiser and the schedule's
constructor does not list the member, but the early return is forced by the
`< 0` clause rather than by that zero.

This adds a straight line for `loopCount == 1` -- preProcess(0), barrier,
midProcess(0), barrier, postProcess(0) -- and leaves every other loop count on
the original path, unchanged line for line.

Decode never has more than one chunk. mLimit is
`(USER_WORKSPACE_LIMIT / DOUBLE_WORKSPACE_SPLIT) / (K + DOUBLE_ROW * N *
SIZE_OF_HALF_2)`, which for one TP16 shard of a 6144-wide model with N=256 is
33554432 / 7168 = 4681, so `Ceil(M, mLimit)` only reaches 2 at M=4682. Batch
one with top-8 routing dispatches 8 rows and batch four dispatches 32.

Measured on one Ascend910_93 die, A8W4 MSD, K=6144 N=256, 8 active experts of
256 each holding one row. Both schedules were built into one binary selected
at run time, so the pair shares a process, a device context, one HBM
allocation and one set of weight banks; six independent 192.75 MiB banks
rotate with the active expert window so each batch of 32 calls touches
202.1 MB of distinct weight addresses against a 192 MiB L2. Eager calls to
this operator cost as much on the host as the kernel costs on the device, so
the batch is captured into an ACL graph and replayed; host cost during
replay is 0.72 to 1.48 us per call. Three runs of 40 rounds, arms replayed
A,B,B,A per round:

  original loop     98.153   99.627   97.561 us per call
  straight line     91.735   90.473   92.705
  paired difference -6.426   -9.171   -4.865   (sd 0.442, 0.194, 0.274)

0 positive against 40 negative in each run, p = 1.8e-12. At 32 rows the same
binary gives 114.084 -> 105.175 us, and at 8 experts of 4 rows 143.303 ->
132.367.

Of that saving 3.54 us is the two barriers themselves: replicating the
removed pair fourteen times prices one mixed `SyncAll<false>` at 2.30 us and
one AIV-only `SyncAll<true>` at 1.25 us, and 2.30 + 1.25 agrees with the
3.54 us the replicated pair costs. The remainder is the two dead calls, the
`tempWorkspaceSplitConfig` copy, one extra `pipe->Reset()` and the loop
scaffolding.

Output is unchanged, not merely close: the straight-line binary and the
unmodified one produce bit-identical int8 codes and bit-identical output
scales over the measured shapes, and both sit within one LSB of an
independent host replay of the kernel's arithmetic with the per-row
code maximum at 127.

This reaches `gate_up` only. The `down` projection of the same MoE layer does
not run through this operator -- it calls the CANN built-in
`npu_grouped_matmul` -- so no equivalent saving is available here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Base: unknown
---
--- a/csrc/gmm/grouped_matmul_swiglu_quant_v2/op_kernel/grouped_matmul_swiglu_quant_v2_a8w4_msd_pipeline.h
+++ b/csrc/gmm/grouped_matmul_swiglu_quant_v2/op_kernel/grouped_matmul_swiglu_quant_v2_a8w4_msd_pipeline.h
@@ -97,6 +97,26 @@
     midProcess.Init(gmAddrParams, gmmSwigluQuantV2BaseParams);
     postProcess.Init(gmAddrParams, gmmSwigluQuantV2BaseParams, gmmSwigluQuantV2);
 
+    // batch-one fast path: a single workspace split needs only pre -> mm -> post.
+    if (workspaceSplitConfig.loopCount == 1) {
+        preProcess.Process(workspaceSplitConfig, 0, pipe);
+        UpdateWorkSpaceSplitConfig(workspaceSplitConfig, 0);
+        if ASCEND_IS_AIV {
+            pipe->Reset();
+        }
+        SyncAll<false>();
+        midProcess.Process(workspaceSplitConfig, 0);
+        if ASCEND_IS_AIV {
+            pipe->Reset();
+        }
+        SyncAll<false>();
+        postProcess.Process(workspaceSplitConfig, 0, pipe);
+        if ASCEND_IS_AIV {
+            pipe->Destroy();
+        }
+        return;
+    }
+
     // 1.前处理提前下发一次
     preProcess.Process(workspaceSplitConfig, 0, pipe);
     for (int64_t workspaceSplitLoopIdx = 0; workspaceSplitLoopIdx < workspaceSplitConfig.loopCount;
-- 
2.43.0

